    "transcript": [
      {
        "title": {
          "zh": "第一幕 · 新的巴黎",
          "en": "The new Paris"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "19世纪中叶，奥斯曼把巴黎改造成一座现代城市。卡耶博特选了圣拉扎尔火车站附近一个新建的路口，画下雨中的行人。",
          "en": "In the mid-19th century, Haussmann rebuilt Paris as a modern city. Caillebotte chose a new crossroads near the Gare Saint-Lazare and painted people walking there in the rain."
        }
      },
      {
        "title": {
          "zh": "第二幕 · 1877年的画展",
          "en": "The 1877 exhibition"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "1877年4月，这幅画在第三届印象派画展上展出。那次画展很大程度上是卡耶博特自己组织的。这幅画因为逼真和精确，广受好评。",
          "en": "In April 1877, the painting was shown at the third Impressionist exhibition, which Caillebotte had largely organised himself. It was widely praised for its realism and precision."
        }
      },
      {
        "title": {
          "zh": "第三幕 · 来到芝加哥",
          "en": "In Chicago"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "之后几十年，它一直留在卡耶博特家族手里，很少有人看到。1964年，芝加哥艺术博物馆买下了它，人们才重新认识了卡耶博特。",
          "en": "For decades it stayed in the Caillebotte family, rarely seen. In 1964 the Art Institute of Chicago acquired it, and Caillebotte's work was rediscovered."
        }
      }
    ]
  },
